Z||000002||Springtyme||09-07-2001||11:24 AM||||Alright, I got my basic layout complete, now I'm looking for a cope and GT from every year. As of now, I have an 85 Coupe, 86 GT, 87 Coupe, and my 88 coupe. Any pics of the others are GREATLY appreciated and needed. Also, could anyone tel me what year this car is??? (can you tell I'm bad at telling the years?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/Coupe_w_flames.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> <P>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||09-07-2001||11:34 AM||||That's a tough call because you can't see if the decklid has a hump or not, or if the car has a third brake light.<P>But I think that's an 84.  It looks like the 1/4 window has the thick rubber strip around the outside, which only came on the 84's because they had real glass 1/4 windows instead of plexiglas.<P>I suppose it could be an 87 GT that somebody converted to 84 bodywork, but I doubt it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||09-07-2001||12:11 PM||||It is either an 87 or an 88. First the 1/4 window is the plastic. Glass (84) has a dual trim and is cut differently (slightly smaller) Second it has the smooth trim and the 87/88 nose (no pads). Since it has the 14" wheels and they sit in the wheel well even to the rears I would say it's an 87. 88's had the different suspension and the offset is different between front and rear. So using those wheels the front would look like they are farther out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||09-07-2001||12:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>...Second it has the smooth trim and the 87/88 nose (no pads).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Oreif... I'd have to disagree with you.  I believe it does have the "pads" that were found on 84-86 coupes... not the smoother nose.  The later nose has a smoother, more rounded drop to it than the one shown.  As to the Quarter window glass... they are interchangible- therefore it too isn't a very good reference for year.  They are easily and frequently replaced.  The true determining factors are typically the decklid.  A picture from the back would be greatly helpful in this case.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
