Z||000019||MinnGreenGT||09-07-2001||01:14 PM||||Signs of year by appearance (in stock form):<P>'84 coupe/se  All '84's are "notchbacks" & had 4cyl engines -vent in center of decklid instead of hump. No vents on sides of decklid- plain flat panel. '84 & '85 model year cars have a "grooved" trim all the way around the car.<P>'84 Indy model has "Aero" Nose, red accents, red accented interior- stickers were optional. Wing on decklid. Different rear fascia.<P>'85 coupe/se  All '85's are "notchbacks" -hump in center of decklid, vents on side.<P>'85 GT- Has "Aero" nose and wing on decklid.  Has "GT" on quarter window, and runs 2.8L V6 motor. GT/Indy style rear fascia.<P>'86 coupe - basically same as '85 coupe... maybe someone else knows something specifc & visible. '86 Cars all have the "smooth" trim all the way around the car (not grooved).<P>'86 SE- has "Aero" nose, newer GT-style rear fascia. Wing optional.  Available with either the 4cyl or V6 engines. Typically had black lower "aero package" rocker panels (below the doors).<P>'86 1/2 GT- The first of the "fastback" bodies was release mid-year (hence the 1/2). Wing OR luggage rack optional.  Full "Aero" package including nose, rocker panels, and rear fascia.  Lower Aero trim is painted Metallic Silver/Gray reguardless of body color.<P>'87 coupe- new smoother style front nose (see your car's) and rear fascia. (no "Pads"). Not sure of other distinguishing marks.<P>'87 GT- Same as '86 1/2 GT.  Execpt the V6 engine now has "Fiero" engraved on it instead of a sticker (on earlier models).<P>'88 coupes- about the same as '87 coupes visually.  Visual difference is usually in the "offset" of the wheels- all 88 models had the updated suspension.<P>'88 GT's- maintaining Fastback body style with full "aero" package- see wheel offsets.  Also, the cars are now painted one color for entire body- no color change on lower rocker panels & trim.  T-tops is also a "factory" option (made available by C&C in pontiac michigan) as well as adjustable lumbar seats (rare).<P>'88 Formula- V6 in coupe body with Wing option.  Also "formula" door sticker.  Considered the fastest of stock Fieros due to the lighter weight of the coupe body, with the power of the V6 and newer '88 suspension.  See also wheel "offset.<P>Please don't flame me (anyone) if I've forgotten anything- I'm not perfect!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Hope this was helpful in some way.  Feel free to ask further if necessary!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
