Z||000026||Oreif||09-07-2001||02:18 PM||||OK I copied the pic of the one with flames, Upon playing with brightness and contrast 2 things came up. First I stand corrected it is the 84-86 body style. (bumper pads) Second there is a 3rd brake light housing. You can see the edge of it by zooming in and cutting the brightness down. I would guess it's 86.<P><BR>Here's a pic of my 86 SE:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fcol_01_1.jpg"> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||11
Z||000027||Oreif||09-07-2001||02:35 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Signs of year by appearance (in stock form):<P><BR>'86 coupe - basically same as '85 coupe... maybe someone else knows something specifc & visible. '86 Cars all have the "smooth" trim all the way around the car (not grooved).<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The coupe smooth trim came on with the bumper change in 87. 86 Still has the ribbed/grooved trim.<P>87 SE's are the same as 86 SE's and have ribbed/grooved trim.<P>All other stuff is correct. I'd also like to add:<BR>86 first year of 3rd brake light.<BR>Very late 86 cars came with the getreg 5-spd with the V-6. All previous V-6's had a 4-spd manual.<P>Stock colors are year specific too.<P>84-88 red, black, white, Lt Gray met (silver)<BR>86-87 Gold was added<BR>87 was Blue (only Year)<BR>87-88 Med red metallic<BR>88 Yellow (Only year)<P>Total Fiero's built 1984 to 1988: 370,168<BR>(Includes Indy Pace Cars and Mera's)<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
